{"name":"Captivating","hex":"#d8cace","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"captivating","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["That captivates; fascinating.","Very beautiful or attractive."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of captivate"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/captivating"}],"entries":[{"title":"Captivating","blocks":[{"text":"Captivating: Unveiling the Mystery of a Woman's Soul is a book published in 2005 by John Eldredge and his wife Stasi. The book rejects the idea of an ideal woman and explores biblical scripture from the view that God desires woman to embrace, rather than fear, her femininity. Captivating is a companion to Wild at Heart, also by John Eldredge, and argues that its model of femininity complements men's innate desires for \"a battle to fight,\" \"an adventure to live,\" and \"a beauty to rescue.\" They claim that women have three core desires: \"to be romanced, to play an irreplaceable role in a great adventure, and to unveil beauty\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b0/CaptivatingEldredge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Captivating","wikidata":"Q5036918"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"captivating":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5c/En-us-captivating.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5c/En-us-captivating.ogg/En-us-captivating.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.635625},{"title":"Werner's nomenclature of colours greys"